NAME
    qml-rules - enforce layout-only QML rules for the Qt frontend

SYNOPSIS
    qml-rules [--fixture] <path>...

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.dev module that checks .qml files against the
    Qt frontend's separation rule: QML arranges layout, binds properties,
    and invokes model methods while Rust owns logic and text. Each
    <path> may be a .qml file or a directory searched recursively
    ('target' directories are skipped).

    Findings print one per line as 'file:line rule words', followed by a
    final summary line ('ok' or 'N findings'). Checked rules:

        function     Any QML function definition other than a
                     Connections handler whose body is a single call
                     ('function onX(...) { target.call() }').
        callLater    Use of Qt.callLater.
        literal      An array or object literal constructed in QML.
        words        User-visible string literals outside exempt named
                     bindings (objectName, role, font.family, source,
                     fragmentShader, vertexShader, property, properties,
                     pragma, Accessible.role, placeholderText, sequence,
                     contextType) and colour literals ('#rrggbb',
                     'transparent').
        onCompleted  Component.onCompleted doing more than requesting
                     focus.
        rows         A ListModel containing ListElement rows.
        import       An import outside the allowed view prefixes
                     (QtQuick, QtQuick.Controls, QtQuick.Templates,
                     QtQuick.Layouts, QtQuick.Shapes, QtQml including
                     QtQml.Models, EmuSen., QtMultimedia), a forbidden
                     import (QtQuick.LocalStorage), or EmuSen.Kit
                     imported without an alias ('import EmuSen.Kit as
                     Kit').

OPTIONS
    --fixture
        Treat <path>... as test or gallery fixtures whose inline words,
        ListModel rows, and array/object literals stand in for live
        models; disables the words, rows, and literal rules while
        enforcing all others.

EXAMPLES
    qml-rules Frontend/kit-qt
    qml-rules --fixture Frontend/qt-test/qml Frontend/kit-gallery/qml
    qml-rules Frontend/themes/emusen/screens/Home.qml

EXIT STATUS
    0   No findings.
    1   One or more findings reported.
    2   Missing or invalid path, or unknown option.

SEE ALSO
    theme-check(1), esde-check(1), dupes(1)
